# This folder holds the application: code, configuration, private storage and
# the installer. None of it is ever served over HTTP.
#
# It matters because cPanel forces a document root under public_html, so this
# directory is reachable laterally through the account's main domain - for
# example https://veloraweb.com/crewvia/ - even though the subdomain's own
# document root is public/ one level down.
#
# public/.htaccess grants access back for that one directory. Both files ship
# in the archive on purpose: adding them by hand after extraction is how the
# protection gets silently overwritten by the next deployment.
Require all denied

<FilesMatch "^\.ht">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

Options -Indexes
